    <main id="top">
    <section class="hero desktop" id="hero" aria-labelledby="h1">
      <div class="sheet plate">
        <h1 id="h1">Clean up your Gmail inbox on your Mac.</h1>
        <p class="lede">zero is a Mac app that keeps the emails you need to deal with and archives the rest. Undo any archive. Keep using Gmail or Apple Mail.</p>
        <div class="acts">
          <a class="btn default" href="#install">Install zero for Mac</a>
          <a class="textlink" href="https://zero.headless.com/install.sh">Read the installer first</a>
        </div>
        <p class="req">Apple Silicon. macOS 26 or later. Gmail only.</p>
      </div>
    
      <p class="sr-only">Illustration: zero's menu-bar window shows Run zero now, then Working…. While it works, zero selects eight routine emails in a Gmail inbox shown as a Mac list window and drags them into a dated Auto-Archived folder. Four emails that need a reply or action stay. The Trash stays empty.</p>
    
